A||N||4||TRL46202||Help with Vin Number||||1||
Z||000000||TRL46202||08-26-2000||12:17 AM||||Can anyone tell me how to tell with the vin what number in the production line was the Fiero I'm thinking about getting. This guy said it was #26 in line in 1986. I don't believe him because he also said he was the 2nd owner nad it has 110,000 on it. He is the 6th owner and the Auto Auction before him had it listed at 135,000 in 1997 and he titled it with 113,000 in 1998. Strange?  I want to get all the facts before I go to see the car and also he claims it has a rare 2.8 chevy engine and all the other fieros can off the line with the standard Pontiac engine? I've had a few GT's in my time but I think this guy is on crack. Thanks for any help.<P>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-26-2000||12:28 AM||||Here is a typical '88 VIN (I don't own any other year)<P>1G2PG1190JP213007<P><BR>This '88 Fiero (my first!) was #13007 out of 26,402 built in '88<P><BR>The last 5 digits tells you the build sequence.....that means the last 6 numbers of this '86 GT's VIN should read 200026.<P>All V-6 Fieros have Chevy engines.....there is no such thing as a Pontiac V-6 in a Fiero.  <P>It sounds like someone played with the odometer on this car too.  I'd be very leary about doing business with this person.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-26-2000||12:43 AM||||It sounds like he O.D.'d on crack. I wouldn't buy the car from him because it sounds like he's trying to get way more money for it than it's really worth. You can go to the Carfax site and run the VIN to get a history on the car. I think it costs some money but if you really want the car it might be worth it.<P>WOW so my car is the 2,814th car to roll off the assembly line for 86 Fiero's. I wonder if anyone here has the 2813th or 2815th?<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-26-2000).]||||reg||1
